\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Token and sequence negative log-likelihood}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{pretraining}
\tag{loss}

\p{For a token string #{x_{1:n}}, the \newvocab{token negative
log-likelihood} at position #{t} is
##{
\ell_t(\theta;x_{1:n})
=-\log\pi_\theta(x_t\mid x_{<t}).
}
The \newvocab{sequence negative log-likelihood} is the declared aggregation
##{
\ell(\theta;x_{1:n})
=\sum_{t\in I(x_{1:n})}\ell_t(\theta;x_{1:n}),
}
where #{I(x_{1:n})} is the set of positions included by the training mask.}

\p{The decoder-only training algorithm in
\citet{sec. 7}{phuong2022formal} uses cross-entropy against target tokens.
For a one-hot target, that cross-entropy is the displayed negative
log-likelihood. Keeping #{I(x_{1:n})} explicit records whether padding,
prompt tokens, or other positions are excluded.}
